Runs, Schedule, Content tabs + run control (stop/steer/approvals)

Run control (the layer promised after the tool timeline):
- Chat Stop now stops the real run on the gateway via run_stop, not just the
  client stream; the run id is captured from the run event
- approval prompts render in-thread with choice buttons, POST to the run
  approval endpoint
- steer endpoint wired

New tabs, all real data:
- Runs: execution history from the agent log, filter to failures, failed
  rows highlighted (surfaces the server's 3 failed runs)
- Schedule: Hermes cron jobs, with schedule, next run, last status, and any
  error surfaced; dict-shaped schedules normalised to their display form
- Content: agent output library, filter by author, markdown reader

Backend: cron_jobs / content_docs / content_read in the data layer; new
endpoints for schedule, content read, and run stop/steer/approval.
Verified on the server: 1 cron job with its error surfaced, 21 content docs
rendering; on WSL both are honest-empty.

